WEBVTT

00:00:00.261 --> 00:00:02.248
Here are two curves on the same axes,

00:00:02.830 --> 00:00:04.878
y equals e to the x, and y

00:00:04.999 --> 00:00:05.922
equals two to the x.

00:00:06.504 --> 00:00:08.239
Both cross the y axis at a height

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:08.400
of one.

00:00:09.487 --> 00:00:10.931
E to the x leaves that point with

00:00:10.992 --> 00:00:13.077
a slope of exactly one, because it's its

00:00:13.178 --> 00:00:13.759
own derivative.

00:00:14.465 --> 00:00:16.119
But two to the x is flatter there.

00:00:16.603 --> 00:00:18.151
So the derivative of two to the x

00:00:18.253 --> 00:00:19.660
can't just be two to the x.

00:00:20.428 --> 00:00:20.981
Then what is it?

00:00:21.769 --> 00:00:22.693
Here's the strange part.

00:00:23.197 --> 00:00:25.045
The answer contains a logarithm.

00:00:25.749 --> 00:00:27.153
Why would a log turn up when you

00:00:27.195 --> 00:00:28.559
differentiate an exponential?

00:00:29.297 --> 00:00:31.414
Last video gave us a measuring stick.

00:00:31.899 --> 00:00:33.572
Divide the gradient by the height.

00:00:34.399 --> 00:00:36.405
For e to the x, that ratio is

00:00:36.567 --> 00:00:36.987
always one.

00:00:37.973 --> 00:00:39.701
Squash the curve to e to the two

00:00:39.862 --> 00:00:41.992
x, and the ratio is always two.

00:00:43.036 --> 00:00:45.701
Whenever the power is some number times x,

00:00:46.143 --> 00:00:48.487
the gradient is that number times the height.

00:00:49.091 --> 00:00:51.045
So the ratio tells you the number in

00:00:51.086 --> 00:00:51.549
the power.

00:00:52.375 --> 00:00:54.246
Let's measure two to the x that way.

00:00:55.636 --> 00:00:58.071
Start at x equals zero, where the height

00:00:58.193 --> 00:00:58.574
is one.

00:00:59.297 --> 00:01:01.800
Slide a second point in towards it, and

00:01:01.821 --> 00:01:03.422
the secant's slope settles:

00:01:04.064 --> 00:01:06.246
point eight three, point seven two,

00:01:06.768 --> 00:01:07.869
point six nine six.

00:01:08.672 --> 00:01:10.998
The tangent's slope is about point six nine

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:11.299
three.

00:01:12.188 --> 00:01:12.959
Now move along.

00:01:13.564 --> 00:01:16.048
At x equals one, the height is two,

00:01:16.570 --> 00:01:18.553
and the gradient is about one point three

00:01:18.614 --> 00:01:18.894
nine.

00:01:19.677 --> 00:01:21.865
At x equals two, the height is four,

00:01:22.228 --> 00:01:24.175
and the gradient is about two point seven

00:01:24.236 --> 00:01:24.496
seven.

00:01:25.220 --> 00:01:27.607
The gradient is always the same fraction of

00:01:27.649 --> 00:01:28.029
the height.

00:01:28.593 --> 00:01:31.048
The ratio stays at point six nine three.

00:01:31.673 --> 00:01:33.683
That's the pattern we saw for e to

00:01:33.704 --> 00:01:34.970
a number times x.

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:36.894
Try three to the x.

00:01:37.618 --> 00:01:39.822
Now the ratio settles at about one point

00:01:39.883 --> 00:01:42.689
zero nine nine, the same at every point.

00:01:43.513 --> 00:01:46.010
So each base has its own fixed ratio.

00:01:46.694 --> 00:01:49.181
Two gives about point six nine, three gives

00:01:49.222 --> 00:01:50.204
about one point one.

00:01:51.127 --> 00:01:53.471
Somewhere between two and three, there must be

00:01:53.512 --> 00:01:55.736
a base with a ratio of exactly one.

00:01:56.680 --> 00:01:58.610
Slide the base from two up to three,

00:01:59.033 --> 00:02:00.259
and watch the ratio climb.

00:02:00.963 --> 00:02:03.130
At two point seven one eight, it reads

00:02:03.452 --> 00:02:03.592
one,

00:02:04.134 --> 00:02:06.040
and the curve lands right on top of

00:02:06.061 --> 00:02:06.863
e to the x.

00:02:07.488 --> 00:02:08.780
That base is e.

00:02:09.811 --> 00:02:10.881
So what are these numbers?

00:02:11.609 --> 00:02:13.537
Plot each ratio against its base.

00:02:14.081 --> 00:02:15.848
Two gives point six nine three.

00:02:16.553 --> 00:02:17.285
E gives one.

00:02:17.813 --> 00:02:20.583
Three gives one point zero nine nine, and

00:02:20.705 --> 00:02:22.732
four gives one point three eight six.

00:02:23.456 --> 00:02:25.179
These points sit on a curve you met

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:27.526
in Year 11, the natural log curve.

00:02:28.231 --> 00:02:29.164
Check it on a calculator.

00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:31.765
The natural log of two is point six

00:02:31.806 --> 00:02:32.308
nine three.

00:02:32.893 --> 00:02:34.719
So the gradient of a to the x

00:02:35.102 --> 00:02:37.511
is always the natural log of a, times

00:02:37.552 --> 00:02:37.912
the height.

00:02:38.516 --> 00:02:40.424
But why would a logarithm be the answer?

00:02:41.088 --> 00:02:42.432
The key is to write two as a

00:02:42.494 --> 00:02:42.995
power of e.

00:02:44.019 --> 00:02:45.683
The natural log of two is the power

00:02:45.704 --> 00:02:47.308
you raise e to, to get two.

00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:50.417
So two is approximately e to the point

00:02:50.459 --> 00:02:51.140
six nine three.

00:02:52.004 --> 00:02:54.573
Exactly, two to the x is e raised

00:02:54.614 --> 00:02:56.560
to the power x times the natural log

00:02:56.581 --> 00:02:56.922
of two.

00:02:57.625 --> 00:02:59.209
So two to the x is just e

00:02:59.551 --> 00:03:01.214
to the x, stretched sideways.

00:03:02.198 --> 00:03:04.103
Watch this tangent triangle on e to the

00:03:04.224 --> 00:03:05.326
x, at height two.

00:03:06.170 --> 00:03:08.074
Stretch it sideways by a factor of one

00:03:08.115 --> 00:03:10.440
point four four, and the run grows from

00:03:10.702 --> 00:03:12.867
one to one point four four, while the

00:03:12.948 --> 00:03:14.150
rise stays two.

00:03:14.893 --> 00:03:17.597
So at every height, the slope is multiplied

00:03:17.638 --> 00:03:19.019
by point six nine three,

00:03:19.621 --> 00:03:21.724
and the gradient becomes point six nine three

00:03:21.845 --> 00:03:22.565
times the height.

00:03:23.542 --> 00:03:25.897
Now let's prove it for any positive base

00:03:26.118 --> 00:03:26.219
a.

00:03:26.862 --> 00:03:28.828
The natural log of a is the power

00:03:28.868 --> 00:03:32.258
that turns e into a, so a equals

00:03:32.479 --> 00:03:33.803
e to the natural log of a.

00:03:34.545 --> 00:03:36.614
So a to the x is e raised

00:03:36.654 --> 00:03:37.477
to a new power,

00:03:37.979 --> 00:03:39.545
x times the natural log of a.

00:03:40.269 --> 00:03:41.032
Call that power u.

00:03:42.138 --> 00:03:44.101
The base is fixed, so the natural log

00:03:44.142 --> 00:03:45.303
of a is just a number,

00:03:45.845 --> 00:03:47.667
and d u by d x is the

00:03:47.708 --> 00:03:48.549
natural log of a.

00:03:49.312 --> 00:03:51.498
And d y by d u is e

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:51.900
to the u.

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:54.112
The chain rule multiplies them.

00:03:54.756 --> 00:03:56.624
Put the power back, and that e to

00:03:56.644 --> 00:03:58.332
the u is a to the x again.

00:03:59.215 --> 00:04:01.062
So the derivative of a to the x

00:04:01.484 --> 00:04:03.752
is the natural log of a, times a

00:04:03.773 --> 00:04:04.234
to the x.

00:04:05.039 --> 00:04:06.284
Try a equals e.

00:04:06.968 --> 00:04:08.992
The natural log of e is one, so

00:04:09.033 --> 00:04:10.716
you get e to the x back, the

00:04:10.757 --> 00:04:11.638
rule you already know.

00:04:12.368 --> 00:04:14.316
What if the base is less than two?

00:04:15.021 --> 00:04:15.706
Slide it down.

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:18.718
At a equals one, the curve flattens into

00:04:18.759 --> 00:04:21.669
the line y equals one, with gradient zero.

00:04:22.313 --> 00:04:24.118
The rule agrees, because the natural log of

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:25.142
one is zero.

00:04:25.886 --> 00:04:27.432
Keep going to a half.

00:04:28.137 --> 00:04:29.028
Now the curve falls.

00:04:29.616 --> 00:04:31.419
The natural log of a half is minus

00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:33.964
point six nine three, so the gradient is

00:04:34.125 --> 00:04:36.208
negative, while the height stays positive.

00:04:36.851 --> 00:04:38.654
A half to the x is two to

00:04:38.675 --> 00:04:40.919
the minus x, the mirror image of two

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:41.420
to the x.

00:04:42.184 --> 00:04:43.671
And the base must be positive.

00:04:44.295 --> 00:04:46.578
The natural log of a negative number doesn't

00:04:46.619 --> 00:04:46.919
exist,

00:04:47.461 --> 00:04:49.404
and a negative base can't be raised to

00:04:49.505 --> 00:04:50.025
every power.

00:04:50.821 --> 00:04:53.167
Find the gradient of y equals two to

00:04:53.207 --> 00:04:55.111
the x at x equals three.

00:04:55.998 --> 00:04:57.131
Here the base is two.

00:04:57.736 --> 00:05:00.048
Copy two to the x, then multiply by

00:05:00.088 --> 00:05:01.214
the natural log of two.

00:05:01.917 --> 00:05:04.142
So d y by d x is the

00:05:04.202 --> 00:05:06.527
natural log of two, times two to the

00:05:06.687 --> 00:05:06.807
x.

00:05:07.830 --> 00:05:10.256
At x equals three, two cubed is eight,

00:05:10.618 --> 00:05:12.823
so the gradient is eight times the natural

00:05:12.864 --> 00:05:13.565
log of two,

00:05:14.308 --> 00:05:15.731
about five point five five.

00:05:16.774 --> 00:05:18.658
On the graph, the height is eight, and

00:05:18.679 --> 00:05:21.344
the gradient is point six nine three times

00:05:21.385 --> 00:05:21.565
that.

00:05:22.348 --> 00:05:23.959
If you wrote just two to the x,

00:05:24.242 --> 00:05:24.905
you'd get eight.

00:05:25.629 --> 00:05:27.355
That's the slope e to the x has

00:05:27.476 --> 00:05:28.017
at that height.

00:05:28.784 --> 00:05:29.736
Here's a way to remember it.

00:05:30.382 --> 00:05:31.745
Except when the base is one, a

00:05:32.467 --> 00:05:34.111
to the x is e to the x

00:05:34.292 --> 00:05:35.394
scaled sideways.

00:05:36.077 --> 00:05:37.804
The natural log of the base sets the

00:05:37.824 --> 00:05:38.126
scale.

00:05:38.832 --> 00:05:40.166
You can see that number on the graph.

00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:42.559
Where a to the x crosses the y

00:05:42.659 --> 00:05:44.428
axis, its height is one.

00:05:45.152 --> 00:05:47.244
So its slope there is exactly the natural

00:05:47.304 --> 00:05:47.787
log of a.

00:05:48.854 --> 00:05:50.758
Two to the x leaves with slope point

00:05:50.819 --> 00:05:51.600
six nine three,

00:05:52.363 --> 00:05:54.046
and e to the x with slope one.

00:05:54.829 --> 00:05:57.375
So copy the exponential, then multiply by the

00:05:57.457 --> 00:05:58.679
natural log of the base.

00:06:01.391 --> 00:06:01.855
Your turn.

00:06:02.318 --> 00:06:04.281
For f of x equals five to the

00:06:04.463 --> 00:06:07.247
x, find f prime of x, then the

00:06:07.328 --> 00:06:09.752
exact value of f prime of zero.

00:06:10.316 --> 00:06:11.223
Pause here to answer.

00:06:21.968 --> 00:06:24.557
The base is five, so f prime of

00:06:24.618 --> 00:06:26.966
x is the natural log of five, times

00:06:27.028 --> 00:06:27.770
five to the x.

00:06:28.553 --> 00:06:29.073
At zero,

00:06:29.615 --> 00:06:31.879
five to the zero is one, so f

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:34.444
prime of zero is exactly the natural log

00:06:34.485 --> 00:06:36.408
of five, about one point six one.

00:06:37.271 --> 00:06:39.013
If you wrote x times five to the

00:06:39.115 --> 00:06:41.860
x minus one, that's the power rule, and

00:06:41.921 --> 00:06:42.962
it needs x in the base.

00:06:43.585 --> 00:06:45.759
It gives zero here, a flat tangent on

00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:46.524
a rising curve.

00:06:48.016 --> 00:06:48.399
Last one.

00:06:48.945 --> 00:06:51.126
For g of x equals a half to

00:06:51.147 --> 00:06:54.048
the x, find the exact value of g

00:06:54.109 --> 00:06:56.830
prime of two, and explain its sign.

00:06:57.515 --> 00:06:58.407
Pause here to answer.

00:07:09.061 --> 00:07:11.166
G prime of x is the natural log

00:07:11.206 --> 00:07:13.311
of a half, times a half to the

00:07:13.532 --> 00:07:13.672
x.

00:07:14.594 --> 00:07:16.596
At two, a half squared is a quarter,

00:07:17.016 --> 00:07:19.238
so g prime of two is a quarter

00:07:19.438 --> 00:07:21.540
of the natural log of a half, which

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:23.901
is minus the natural log of two, over

00:07:23.961 --> 00:07:24.222
four.

00:07:24.942 --> 00:07:26.964
It's negative because the base is less than

00:07:27.184 --> 00:07:29.866
one, so its natural log is negative, while

00:07:29.906 --> 00:07:31.647
a half to the x is always positive.

00:07:32.349 --> 00:07:34.175
Writing the natural log of two there gives

00:07:34.217 --> 00:07:34.959
the wrong sign.

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:38.403
So a to the x is e with

00:07:38.663 --> 00:07:40.425
x times the natural log of a in

00:07:40.445 --> 00:07:40.886
the power,

00:07:41.406 --> 00:07:43.088
and its derivative is the natural log of

00:07:43.108 --> 00:07:44.830
a, times a to the x.

00:07:45.873 --> 00:07:46.114
Next:

00:07:46.716 --> 00:07:49.024
our ratio points traced the natural log curve.

00:07:49.747 --> 00:07:51.598
What's the gradient of that curve itself?

00:07:54.295 --> 00:07:55.158
Here are the key notes.

00:07:55.561 --> 00:07:57.108
Pause the video if you need more time

00:07:57.150 --> 00:07:57.611
to copy them.
